<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali ibn Abi Talib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">caliph <a href="/years/656">656</a>–<a href="/years/661">661 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hashim">Banu Hashim</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali ibn Abi Talib was the cousin and son-in-law of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> and the fourth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>, ruling from 656 to 661 CE. His caliphate was marked by civil war, including conflict with Mu'awiya, who went on to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> after Ali's assassination. Shia Muslims regard him as the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>, and loyalty to his family later helped mobilise support for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution">Abbasid Revolution</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-abi-talib.jpg" alt="Ali ibn Abi Talib" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: عبدالعزيز علي · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_ten_to_whom_Paradise_was_promised_(Ali).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Into this country came Idris ibn Abdallah, a great-grandson of Hasan ibn Ali and so a descendant of <b>Ali ibn Abi Talib</b> and Fatima, the daughter of the prophet Muhammad.</blockquote><a href="/empire/idrisid-dynasty">Idrisid dynasty · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Ali ibn Abi Talib</b>’s troubled caliphate from 656 to 661 CE, dominated by the First Fitna, the civil war between Ali and the governor of Syria, Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, over responsibility for Uthman’s murder, showed that the caliphate lacked mechanisms for resolving elite political conflict without resort…</blockquote><a href="/empire/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The Umayyad Caliphate was established in 661 CE after the assassination of <b>Ali ibn Abi Talib</b>, the fourth of the Rashidun caliphs and the cousin and son-in-law of the Prophet Muhammad, when Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, the long-serving governor of Syria and the most powerful figure in the…</blockquote><a href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Kharijite Ibn Muljam struck the fourth caliph, <b>Ali ibn Abi Talib</b>, with a poisoned sword as he prayed in the Great Mosque of Kufa.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-26">26 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>At Siffin on the Euphrates, Caliph <b>Ali ibn Abi Talib</b> fought Muawiya, governor of Syria.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-26">26 July in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The early Musha'sha held extreme (ghulat) Shia beliefs: Muhammad's son Mawla Ali claimed that <b>Ali ibn Abi Talib</b> was divine and sacked Najaf in 1453.</blockquote><a href="/state/mushasha">Musha'sha</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=21.42,39.83&amp;year=659" aria-label="Mecca on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5620 1372 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ali ibn Abi Talib"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6070 1642h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6070 1642h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=21.42,39.83&amp;year=659">What was here in 659 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
